1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:04,992
This video shows you how to copy a pipeline,

2
00:00:04,992 --> 00:00:08,350
and what it needs, from one leader to another.

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:11,871
A second leader, staging, has nothing built yet.

4
00:00:11,871 --> 00:00:14,470
Copy the checkout pipeline to it.

5
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:18,710
On this leader, select Export on checkout-parse's row.

6
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:23,728
The export holds the pipeline, and the pipelines it calls.

7
00:00:23,728 --> 00:00:25,910
Here, that's stamp-ecs.

8
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:29,259
Turn on Include routes, sources and destinations,

9
00:00:29,259 --> 00:00:33,190
to take its route, and what the route reads and writes.

10
00:00:33,240 --> 00:00:34,489
Download the file.

11
00:00:34,489 --> 00:00:39,110
It names secrets and certificates, but never holds their values.

12
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:44,190
On staging, open Build, Pipelines, and select Import.

13
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:47,386
Import into Shared, and choose the file.

14
00:00:47,386 --> 00:00:51,290
smeltr asks for a branch: import-checkout.

15
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:53,720
Each object is New here.

16
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:56,959
Untick any you want to leave out.

17
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:57,842
Import.

18
00:00:57,842 --> 00:01:01,102
It's one save on your branch.

19
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,350
Review it, and deploy it, like any other change.

20
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,251
Check on learning.

21
00:01:08,451 --> 00:01:09,938
You import a pipeline.

22
00:01:09,938 --> 00:01:13,377
When do the workers on that leader run it?

23
00:01:17,777 --> 00:01:19,299
Once you deploy it.

24
00:01:19,299 --> 00:01:23,262
The import lands on a branch, as one save.

25
00:01:24,162 --> 00:01:25,449
That's the course.

26
00:01:25,449 --> 00:01:30,698
You can now split, deliver, share, group and move your pipelines.
